# WordPress API Configuration
# This file contains environment variables for WordPress API integration

# WordPress Backend URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORDPRESS_API_URL=http://localhost/candle/

# API Endpoints (will be constructed from base URL)
# /wp-json/jwt-auth/v1/token - JWT Login endpoint
# /wp-json/wc/v3/customers - WooCommerce Customer Registration & Profile endpoint

# Note: Make sure your WordPress site has the following plugins installed:
# 1. JWT Authentication for WP-API - For JWT token authentication
# 2. WooCommerce - For customer registration, profiles, and orders
# 3. Custom post types setup (if using for products)

# WooCommerce REST API Details:
# - Customer Registration: POST /wp-json/wc/v3/customers
# - Customer Profile: GET /wp-json/wc/v3/customers/{id}
# - Update Customer: PUT /wp-json/wc/v3/customers/{id}
# - List Customers: GET /wp-json/wc/v3/customers

# For development, you can add this to your .env.local file
